8. Create AWS Resources Using CLI
Create IAM User
aws iam create-user --user-name dev-user
Create IAM Group
aws iam create-group --group-name Developers
Add User to Group
aws iam add-user-to-group \
  --group-name Developers \
  --user-name dev-user
Create IAM Role
aws iam create-role \
  --role-name EC2-S3-Role \
  --assume-role-policy-document file://trust-policy.json
Create S3 Bucket
aws s3api create-bucket \
  --bucket my-demo-bucket-12345 \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=ap-south-1
Create EC2 Instance
aws ec2 run-instances \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --image-id ami-xxxxxxxx \
  --instance-type t3.micro \
  --key-name my-key \
  --security-group-ids sg-xxxxxxxx \
  --subnet-id subnet-xxxxxxxx
9. IAM Role for EC2
How does an application running on EC2 access S3 without access keys?

Use an IAM Role attached to the EC2 instance.

EC2
 ↓
IAM Role
 ↓
S3 Permissions
 ↓
S3

The application obtains temporary credentials through the EC2 Instance Metadata Service.

Interview Answer

Attach an IAM role to the EC2 instance with the required S3 permissions. The application can obtain temporary credentials from the instance metadata service instead of storing long-lived access keys.

10. AWS Organizations
What is AWS Organizations?

AWS Organizations allows you to centrally manage multiple AWS accounts.

AWS Organization
│
├── Management Account
├── Production Account
├── Development Account
└── Security Account
Benefits
Centralized account management
Organizational Units
Service Control Policies
Consolidated Billing
Centralized Governance
11. What is the Root Account?

The Root in AWS Organizations is the top-level container for all AWS accounts and OUs in the organization.

Organization Root
│
├── Production OU
│   ├── Account
│   └── Account
│
└── Development OU
    └── Account

Note: Do not confuse the Organizations Root with the AWS Account Root User.

12. What is an OU?

OU = Organizational Unit

An OU is a logical container used to organize AWS accounts.

Organization
│
├── Production OU
│   ├── Prod Account
│   └── Prod Account
│
├── Development OU
│   ├── Dev Account
│   └── Dev Account
│
└── Security OU
    └── Security Account

OUs are commonly used to apply governance policies to multiple AWS accounts.

13. What is SCP?

SCP = Service Control Policy

An SCP is an AWS Organizations policy that defines the maximum available permissions for AWS accounts in an organization or OU.

Example

If an account has:

AdministratorAccess

But the SCP denies:

ec2:TerminateInstances

The user cannot terminate EC2 instances.

IAM Policy
    +
SCP
    ↓
Effective Permissions
Important Point

SCP does not grant permissions. It sets the maximum permissions that an account can use.

Example
Organization
│
└── Production OU
    │
    └── Production Account
        │
        ├── IAM Policies
        └── SCP

If the SCP denies an action, an IAM policy cannot override that denial.
